# A loop whose choice weight is written as a fraction: the loop stops with probability 1/2
# per round, so it terminates almost surely and the termination probability is at most 1.
# The weights 1/2 and 1 - 1/2 must reach the QFL equation as numbers; left as a division
# while the body was normalised, (1 - 1/2) * X became X - X * 1/2, an unknown under a
# subtraction, and the reduction was refused as not a QFL input.
# Expected: valid.
nat b;
b := 1;
while (b = 1) {
	{
		b := 0;
	}[1/2]{
		skip
	}
}
?Ex [1] <= 1
